+## Failed session setup
+
+The cleanup hook may run even when setup did not finish. A deployer should release only resources that `beforeSession` actually acquired.
+
+- A throw from `beforeSession` reaches the caller unchanged and fires both `onError` and `afterSession` ([validated by: runs onError and afterSession when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSession.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+- Both hooks receive the same session; `onError` receives the original error and runs before `afterSession`, without starting the provider ([validated by: passes the original error and session to onError before afterSession without starting the provider](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSessionFailure.test.ts#L8)).
+- On this path, setup may have acquired some resources, but no user-input hook, model call, or tool call has run; `afterSession` must tolerate a partially initialized session ([validated by: passes the original error and session to onError before afterSession without starting the provider](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.beforeSessionFailure.test.ts#L8)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+The following properties are separate changes owned by no issue in this epic.
 
-- `beforeSession` is awaited before the `try` block opens ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L91](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L91)), so a throw there escapes before the `catch`/`finally` exist and skips both `onError` and `afterSession`.
 - The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
 - `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
